show_qr.description:
Make sure the whole code is on screen (scroll up) before scanning.

{qr_image}

This QR works **once, for 10 minutes** (until {expires_at}), for {phone_name}. It carries a one-time code, not a password. Unless you chose manual Tailscale enrollment it also carries a single-use Tailscale key (valid ten minutes, one hour with Approve in Tailscale).{manual_note}{reenroll_note}

**Away from home, over Tailscale,** this phone connects to {ha_dial}.

Expired or not scanned? Choose Enroll a device again with the same name: the new QR replaces this one. The phone must reach this Home Assistant when it scans (for example on the home Wi-Fi); if the app says it cannot, it offers a registration string: paste it under Portico > Push ring notification > Configure > "Add a phone's registration". When you remove this phone, also remove its machine in the Tailscale admin console (Machines).

